  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Le présentoir de quincaillerie (the hardware-store peg-hook display)",
    "overview": "The organization is a wall in a hardware store. A perforated galvanized steel pegboard fills the frame, a black sign hangs from two hooks and names the workshop, and each tool hangs below it on its own peg hook as a blister pack you can take home in one line. Each pack shows the real tool through its clear window, names itself on the card and puts its install command on the black price strip.\n\nThe world is photographed retail stock, not illustration: real steel mottling, punched holes, chrome hooks, vacuum-formed plastic with a sheen, soft cast shadows. Colour belongs to the packs alone; everything else is steel, black and clear plastic. The page stays sober and concrete: a workshop rather than a company.\n\nEvery surface is a single composed raster (`profile/assets/wall.jpg`, 1920 x 1280), assembled from plates by `assets/build/render.py` through the HTML compositor `assets/build/wall.html` at a 1536 x 1024 layout rendered at 1.25x. All values below are layout px at 1536; multiply by 1.25 for the shipped JPEG.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One steel pegboard, one hole pitch, every hook on a hole.",
      "One saturated colour per tool, nowhere else.",
      "Real tool imagery in every window; no invented text on any pack.",
      "The install line is the loudest line on each pack, set like a price strip.",
      "Real, selectable text lives below the banner in GitHub's own Markdown."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Colour Per Pack Rule",
        "body": "Each tool owns exactly one saturated colour, used on its card and nowhere else on the wall. The sign, the board, the hooks and the strips stay steel, black and clear.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ink By Contrast Rule",
        "body": "Card ink is black (`#141414`) unless black falls below 4.5:1 on the pack colour, then white. Violet is the only current case (black 3.8:1, white 4.8:1).",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Shared Size Rule",
        "body": "Names fit together and strips fit together: one computed size per role across all packs, so no pack looks louder than another.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Light Rule",
        "body": "One light source for the whole wall; a new object takes the same shadow offset, blur and opacity.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** put every hook ring on a pegboard hole; positions are hole columns, multiples of 68.8px.",
      "**Do** show the real tool in each window: its own screenshot, output or real content.",
      "**Do** keep text on the wall to real names, real contents and real install lines, set by the compositor.",
      "**Do** ship the banner as one opaque composed JPEG with its own background, so it reads the same in GitHub light and dark themes.",
      "**Do** keep everything a reader needs (description, install lines, links) as real Markdown text below the banner."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** print invented text, logos or fake labels on the pack plates; packs carry no text of their own.",
      "**Don't** use a pack colour outside its own pack, or give two tools the same colour.",
      "**Don't** rely on CSS, JavaScript or transparency in the README; GitHub strips the first two and the theme shows through the third."
    ]
  }
}